From: wilkbook packaging
Subject: build: make split-architecture sysmsg headers explicit

This is a build-environment adaptation, not a gVisor runtime fix.  The sysmsg
object macro invokes $(CC) directly from a genrule, so Coral's normal compile
features do not supply Linux UAPI headers.  Select separate Guix-declared
native and AArch64 header flags for the upstream split architecture transition.

--- a/pkg/sentry/platform/systrap/sysmsg/build.bzl
+++ b/pkg/sentry/platform/systrap/sysmsg/build.bzl
@@ -8,7 +8,11 @@ def cc_pie_obj(name, srcs, outs):
         name = name,
         srcs = srcs,
         outs = outs,
-        cmd = "$(CC)  $(CC_FLAGS)  " +
+        cmd = "$(CC)  $(CC_FLAGS)  " + select_arch(
+            amd64 = "$$GVISOR_SYSMSG_NATIVE_INCLUDE_FLAGS ",
+            arm64 = "$$GVISOR_SYSMSG_AARCH64_INCLUDE_FLAGS ",
+            default = "false unsupported-sysmsg-architecture ",
+        ) +
               select({
                   "//tools/bazeldefs:pagesize_64k": " -DPAGE_SIZE=65536 ",
                   "//conditions:default": " -DPAGE_SIZE=4096 ",
